# rsync exclude syntax. Two consumers, both in the "deploy-workshop" job of
# .github/workflows/release.yaml:
#   1. "Stage workshop content (windows)" filters the staged tree with this file
#      (and fails if debug symbols survive), so the uploaded payload is verifiable in CI.
#   2. It is copied into the content root as .deployignore, which the deploy action picks
#      up itself — a manual re-run of the action behaves identically, and the effective
#      rule list shows up in the action log.
#
# The workshop item is the runtime payload every subscriber downloads, so debug/link
# artifacts stay out. The GitHub release zips keep shipping them on purpose (local crash
# symbolization); change the two lists deliberately, never by accident.

# Debug symbols (Injector / plugins / lua51) and link-time artifacts
*.pdb
*.lib
*.exp
*.ilk

# Foreign-platform libraries that the repo commits for the linux/macOS release zips
# (e.g. deps/liblua51.so, deps/liblua51.dylib): the workshop item is the Windows build.
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib

# Plugin manager bookkeeping and runtime leftovers
.ds_plugin_update.lock
update_pending/
test.log
